.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-disputes - Every dispute across accounts, open and closed


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin disputes [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the disputes of every account, newest first, each with the payment it is about
(ids, chain, payer, payee, amount) and both reasons read from the dictionary.

.PP
--status open is what is being contested right now. --reason takes one of the codes a
payer can open a dispute with ('rail0 disputes reasons'); --from and --to bound when the
dispute was opened.

.PP
Read-only: a dispute is opened and closed by the payer, on chain, and a full refund
closes it. 'rail0 admin trace \&' shows one payment's disputes among everything
else that happened to it.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--chain\fP=
	Only disputes on payments of this chain: a slug (arc, base, …) or a chain id; the environment's gateway decides testnet vs mainnet

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	Only disputes opened at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for disputes

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--payment\fP=""
	Only this payment's disputes: its id (UUID) or its rail0_id (0x…)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Only disputes opened with this reason code (see 'rail0 disputes reasons')

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort by opened_at or closed_at (prefix - for descending; default: newest first)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=""
	Only disputes that are open or closed

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	Only disputes opened at/before this ISO-8601 time


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin disputes --status open
  rail0 admin disputes --status open --chain arc --pretty
  rail0 admin disputes --reason not_received --from 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
  rail0 admin disputes --payment 0xrail0Id…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP
